.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Onsager (1944) computed the free energy of the square-lattice Ising model exactly: the first exact solution of a model with a genuine phase transition. Ising2DOnsager evaluates his free energy, internal energy, and heat capacity, together with Yang&#x27;s (1952) spontaneous magnetization m=[1-\sinh^{-4}(2J/k_BT)]^{1/8}. The heat capacity diverges logarithmically at T_c, and the magnetization vanishes with exponent \beta=1/8. Neither the mean-field (Bragg-Williams) theory, shown for comparison, nor Ising&#x27;s own one-dimensional chain reproduces these features.">

